WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 7 Leader Video
Unit 2, Lesson 3: Pantheism

1
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.900
So if naturalism is the dominant view of the West,

2
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.680
pantheism is the dominant view of the East.

3
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.540
Pantheism is interesting,

4
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.300
and it may seem like much of pantheistic thought

5
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.860
is far from your students.

6
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.540
And it, even though it largely dominates

7
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.300
the Eastern culture from Hindus to Buddhists,

8
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.140
and a bunch of others in that part of the world,

9
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.340
it has made its way to the West,

10
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.580
and in a really strange way.

11
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.300
So you might think for your youth group,

12
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.580
well, why are we talking about pantheism?

13
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.260
Why are we bothering with this?

14
00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.700
That's another part of the world,

15
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.380
and I'm not taking my kids on a mission trip over there,

16
00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.940
so do I really need to spend an entire week

17
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.860
dedicated to this sort of Eastern thought?

18
00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.960
Well, do you like Star Wars?

19
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.840
Have you ever heard of karma, meditation, even yoga?

20
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.720
All of these things come from pantheistic thought,

21
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.680
or a pantheistic worldview.

22
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.080
So naturally, we cannot ignore its influence.

23
00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.880
We have to address it, we have to discuss it,

24
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.960
and we gotta get our students to understand

25
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.800
what it exactly is so that they can identify it

26
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.720
and navigate through it successfully.

27
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.360
So what is pantheism?

28
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.600
What are we talking about?

29
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.920
So essentially, think of it this way.

30
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.280
The idea of God, and I'm gonna write God in a small G,

31
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.960
is in all.

32
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.960
Now, you can even say even more specifically, is all.

33
00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.560
We talk about in Christianity,

34
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.000
we talk about the idea of the Holy Spirit

35
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.200
being within us, right?

36
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.280
So God is in us, and that's sort of the idea, right?

37
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.920
Jesus comes, Jesus goes, He sends the Spirit,

38
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.720
the Spirit dwells within us.

39
00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.640
We have this idea of God in us,

40
00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.440
not just God with us, but God in us.

41
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.640
Okay, that's great, but that's not the same thing

42
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.160
when we're talking about pantheism.

43
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.560
We're talking about the idea that God

44
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.440
is literally part of everything.

45
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.000
So there's, so in a pantheistic way,

46
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.440
God would be in me, just as much as in the camera

47
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.220
that I'm speaking to, as this table, as this Bible,

48
00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.720
as this marker, as this whiteboard,

49
00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.480
rocks, trees, pretty much all of it,

50
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:37.450
all of nature is all part of the divine.

51
00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.890
It's all part of who God is.

52
00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:43.970
It's all part of this divine sort of idea of the universe

53
00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.650
that's all combined into one.

54
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.530
There's a divine spark in everything.

55
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.050
It's essentially what pantheism teaches.

56
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.250
So that's where we get this idea of essence or force.

57
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:55.250
When we talk about in Star Wars,

58
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.130
the idea of may the force be with you,

59
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.490
that same kind of idea.

60
00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.650
It's a divine essence that's part of this.

61
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.170
We can call it a force.

62
00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.330
There's something going on behind the scenes

63
00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.050
in everything else.

64
00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.510
So God is present everywhere.

65
00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.130
So it defines life now, it defines life later,

66
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.730
it defines relationships, it defines everything,

67
00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.770
how we see and relate to God.

68
00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.690
But the key I want you to get here

69
00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.090
is the idea of distinction.

70
00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.730
And this is gonna be important

71
00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.150
as you move forward this idea of distinction.

72
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.190
If naturalism is saying there's no God at all,

73
00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.430
pantheism is saying, well, there is God,

74
00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:39.070
but God is not distinct from anything that's created.

75
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.990
That God is a part of creation,

76
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.230
he's a part of you and me,

77
00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.230
it's just as there's no distinction.

78
00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.450
There's no God and us.

79
00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.410
There's just everything all together.

80
00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.270
So for pantheism, there is no distinction at all.

81
00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.990
Okay, so keep that in the back of your mind,

82
00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.230
especially as we move to next week

83
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.790
when we talk about monotheism,

84
00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.910
that's gonna be really, really important.

85
00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:04.630
So in our Bible study portion, we talk about Paul.

86
00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:08.670
We talk about Paul's interaction at the Areopagus

87
00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.030
on Mars Hill.

88
00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:11.870
And we talk about his interaction

89
00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.750
between the Epicureans and the Stoics.

90
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.370
And what's interesting is that these Stoics

91
00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.150
actually believed much of the same kinds of things

92
00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.010
that modern day pantheism believes.

93
00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.230
That idea that God is somehow packed in

94
00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:30.350
every little piece of our world.

95
00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.770
And what Paul does, it's helps them see

96
00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:38.770
that there is a distinction between the two.

97
00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:42.610
That God is here and we are here.

98
00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:43.950
That there's a separation,

99
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.510
that although he's personal,

100
00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.830
although he's right here with us,

101
00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:51.590
he's distinct and other than us.

102
00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.870
And that's incredibly important.

103
00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.910
Because what this does is the loss of distinction

104
00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.830
is actually what leads us to the root of all sin, right?

105
00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.350
Of creating God or creating idols

106
00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.390
that are a substitute for God.

107
00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.350
If you'd say that there's no distinction,

108
00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:14.070
all of these things are just as divine as God.

109
00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.070
So I can worship rocks and trees and everything else.

110
00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.030
It's not any different if we don't have

111
00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.470
some kind of distinction.

112
00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.950
So it drives us right back to the root of our sin.

113
00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.150
It drives us right back to idolatry.

114
00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.710
So your students probably won't see right away,

115
00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.270
but you need to help them begin to see

116
00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.510
how Western culture has actually embraced

117
00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:38.710
a lot of pantheistic ideas about God and creation.

118
00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.870
Again, let's go back to the buffet.

119
00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.510
It's super easy for us to say, wow,

120
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.390
it sounds really cool because I can see

121
00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.230
how beautiful creation is

122
00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:51.110
to want to make that into a God-like thing.

123
00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.350
Or I can treat somebody or an activity

124
00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.030
or I can find a center in myself

125
00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.750
and be the kind of person

126
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.510
and elevate myself to a God-like stature.

127
00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.270
That sounds really cool.

128
00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.270
And along the buffet line,

129
00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.310
sounds like I can say, well,

130
00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.550
if I care about people,

131
00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.990
I can elevate them to that same status too.

132
00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.550
So I like justice.

133
00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.950
That seems to speak to some of my morality.

134
00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.550
That seems, you start to, again,

135
00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.590
go back to that buffet and start to piece things together.

136
00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.350
But when we put them all together,

137
00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.990
we realize once again that this isn't coherent

138
00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.910
and it isn't consistent.

139
00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.390
Now, one quick word of note here

140
00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.710
that I want to make sure that we're clear on.

141
00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.710
If you're doing everything really, really well,

142
00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.830
chances are you have some students

143
00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:48.830
that are either seeking, maybe skeptical,

144
00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.470
and get some questions and are curious.

145
00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.990
And as we're talking about other worldviews,

146
00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.710
whether they believe these things specifically or not,

147
00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:01.510
you want to be careful that we don't offend.

148
00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.550
We want to be careful that we speak truth,

149
00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.590
that we do so in love,

150
00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.270
but that we help understand that these things

151
00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.670
are terribly inconsistent and they don't work.

152
00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.670
But we need to do it without making fun of it.

153
00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.790
We need to do it without making light of it.

154
00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.110
Because when we're talking about worldviews,

155
00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.670
as we talked about a few weeks ago,

156
00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.110
that these things are ingrained in us

157
00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.270
and they are embedded in us,

158
00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.550
and to change is a huge monumental change

159
00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.990
and can often, like we said, create some anxiety.

160
00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.950
So the last thing we want to do

161
00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.990
is invite non-believing students,

162
00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.270
invite our seekers and our skeptics

163
00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.990
into our youth space and say,

164
00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.270
come with your questions,

165
00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.470
come with your curiosity

166
00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.150
and we'll help you navigate

167
00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.310
and we're gonna accept you.

168
00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.390
But at the same time,

169
00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.590
we're gonna sort of make light or make fun

170
00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:53.190
of other worldviews that's not gonna work.

171
00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:57.310
There's, this is a very popular worldview.

172
00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.710
So is naturalism.

173
00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.270
So there's some really, really smart people

174
00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.310
that have said some really, really intelligent things

175
00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.350
about these worldviews.

176
00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.670
Now that doesn't make them true,

177
00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.830
but we have to respect what they believe

178
00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.830
and speak to how it does not line up with reality

179
00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.830
and how it does not line up with truth,

180
00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.590
but do so in love.

181
00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:20.670
So remember, pantheism, God is all.

182
00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.310
God is in everything and a part of everything.

183
00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.710
The rocks, the trees, everything,

184
00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:25.950
and it's divine force.

185
00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.550
And essentially, key word here is

186
00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:32.870
there is no distinction between God and creation,

187
00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.950
between creator and creation.

188
00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.510
And not only does this lead to the idea of idolatry.

189
00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:41.070
If we don't have the distinction,

190
00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:43.190
what does that make God?

191
00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.630
The very fact that we call him God

192
00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.950
means that he is completely distinct,

193
00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:51.750
completely other than and completely holy for us.

194
00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.830
And then, or than us, the idea is

195
00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.510
if God is here and completely other than me,

196
00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.270
I have a standard to look to,

197
00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.550
so I understand what's right and what's wrong.

198
00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.390
I understand what's just and unjust.

199
00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:07.310
I understand the idea of love versus hate.

200
00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.470
Putting God outside of myself

201
00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.390
and making God completely distinct

202
00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.590
helps us navigate reality in a way that makes sense.

203
00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.910
We have to have some kind of distinction.

204
00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.030
It's God who is other than, God who is holy,

205
00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:27.550
God who is supreme creator, overall.

206
00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:31.070
And it's in him that we live and move and have our being.

